## 2. Definitions

For purposes of this License:

### 2.1 Software

**"Software"** means all materials distributed under this License, including, where applicable:

* source code;
* executable code;
* object code;
* scripts;
* service files;
* build files;
* configuration templates;
* documentation;
* data files;
* installation files;
* packaging files; and
* other materials included with the Software.

### 2.2 Licensor

**"Licensor"** means the copyright holder identified in the copyright notice above, its lawful successor, or another person or legal entity expressly authorized to license the Software.

### 2.3 You

**"You"** means an individual or legal entity exercising rights granted under this License.

### 2.4 Modification

**"Modification"** means any change to the Software or any portion of it, including:

* addition;
* deletion;
* replacement;
* editing;
* patching;
* adaptation;
* translation;
* transformation;
* porting;
* alteration of program logic;
* alteration of executable or object code; or
* any other change that produces a modified version of the Software.

Changes expressly permitted under Section 5, **Runtime Configuration and Normal Operation**, are not considered Modifications for purposes of this License.

### 2.5 Derivative Work

**"Derivative Work"** means a work that is based upon, incorporates, adapts, modifies, translates, transforms, or is otherwise legally derived from the Software under applicable copyright law.

### 2.6 Redistribution

**"Redistribution"** means making copies of the Software available to another person or legal entity by any means, including:

* publishing;
* transferring;
* providing copies;
* hosting for download;
* including the Software in another distribution;
* selling copies; or
* otherwise supplying copies to a third party.

### 2.7 Official Package

**"Official Package"** means an executable distribution, installer, binary archive, or update built or expressly approved for release by the Licensor and supplied through an official Autobricks distribution channel. A complete, unmodified copy of such a package redistributed under Section 6 remains an Official Package. A third-party build is not an Official Package merely because its source code, version, name, or output matches an official release.

### 2.8 Build

**"Build"** means compiling, assembling, linking, transpiling, or otherwise transforming source code or intermediate code of the Software into executable code, object code, libraries, test binaries, or installation packages. This includes local builds, automated or CI builds, reproducible builds, and builds for evaluation, testing, or personal use, whether or not the source code is modified. Ordinary installation, unpacking, runtime loading, and configuration of an Official Package as supplied and documented by the Licensor are not Builds.

### 2.9 Unmodified Build

**"Unmodified Build"** means a Build produced from the original source code supplied by the Licensor without editing that source code, implementation scripts, build logic, or dependency declarations. Using documented build options and supported toolchains, and changes to generated artifacts or version metadata made automatically by the supplied build process, do not by themselves constitute a prohibited Modification. This exception does not permit manual source edits, patches, removal of functionality, or weakening of security controls. An Unmodified Build is not an Official Package.

